How to Contribute Support for New PLL Chips
===========================================

Changes
-------
* Find and download the datasheet for the $NEW_PLL PLL to docs/$NEW_PLL.pdf.
* Copy the template file src/pll/pllname.c to src/pll/$NEW_PLL.c.
* Update pllname, pll constants, frequency table fsb_tbl, and pll registers pll_reg in $NEW_PLL.c from the datasheet.
* Modify file src/include/pll.h.
* Add macros PLL_MAKE_FUNCS($NEW_PLL) and PLL_MAKE_STRUCT("$NEW_PLL", $NEW_PLL).

Replace $NEW_PLL with name of the new PLL being added. for example W129C.

Testing
-------
* Build the application.
* Use the print config feature to verify your configuration against the datasheet.
* Test your changes. 
* Use the debug dry run feature to help diagnose issues.

If your changes work, create an issue in Github and submit a pull request. The PR should contain the 3 files above.

